WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.501
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:09.559
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.859 --> 00:00:15.692
Unit three: Family Dynamics. Today you will report what people said with reported speech.

4
00:00:15.992 --> 00:00:18.575
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:22.801
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.150
Communication style.

7
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:29.612
Communication style means the way a person talks and listens.

8
00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:33.075
My dad's communication style is very direct.

9
00:00:33.683 --> 00:00:37.218
Your turn. Say: Communication style.

10
00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:41.613
Communication style.

11
00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:43.398
Role model.

12
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:46.673
Role model means a person you want to be like.

13
00:00:47.283 --> 00:00:49.573
My older sister is my role model.

14
00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.696
Your turn. Say: Role model.

15
00:00:55.533 --> 00:00:56.813
Role model.

16
00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:58.818
Sibling rivalry.

17
00:00:59.817 --> 00:01:03.581
Sibling rivalry means competition between brothers and sisters.

18
00:01:04.183 --> 00:01:06.938
Sibling rivalry is normal in big families.

19
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:10.713
Your turn. Say: Sibling rivalry.

20
00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:15.137
Sibling rivalry.

21
00:01:15.883 --> 00:01:17.511
Parental expectation.

22
00:01:18.517 --> 00:01:22.107
Parental expectation means what parents hope their children will do.

23
00:01:22.717 --> 00:01:25.401
Parental expectation can feel like pressure.

24
00:01:26.017 --> 00:01:29.087
Your turn. Say: Parental expectation.

25
00:01:31.933 --> 00:01:33.747
Parental expectation.

26
00:01:34.483 --> 00:01:35.995
Emotional support.

27
00:01:36.983 --> 00:01:40.132
Emotional support means care and help when you feel bad.

28
00:01:40.717 --> 00:01:43.123
My grandmother gives me emotional support.

29
00:01:43.717 --> 00:01:46.810
Your turn. Say: Emotional support.

30
00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:51.144
Emotional support.

31
00:01:51.883 --> 00:01:53.070
Family value.

32
00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:57.476
Family value means a belief that is important to a family.

33
00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:00.640
Respect is our most important family value.

34
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:04.227
Your turn. Say: Family value.

35
00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:08.207
Family value.

36
00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:10.357
Conflict resolution.

37
00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:14.720
Conflict resolution means ending an argument in a fair way.

38
00:02:15.317 --> 00:02:18.570
We use conflict resolution at the dinner table.

39
00:02:19.183 --> 00:02:21.975
Your turn. Say: Conflict resolution.

40
00:02:24.833 --> 00:02:26.508
Conflict resolution.

41
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.193
Empathy.

42
00:02:29.183 --> 00:02:31.821
Empathy means understanding how others feel.

43
00:02:32.417 --> 00:02:34.765
Empathy helps me understand my brother.

44
00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:37.619
Your turn. Say: Empathy.

45
00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:41.328
Empathy.

46
00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:42.945
Boundary.

47
00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:47.320
Boundary means a limit that protects your space or feelings.

48
00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:50.439
It is fine to set a boundary about your phone.

49
00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:53.656
Your turn. Say: Boundary.

50
00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:57.455
Boundary.

51
00:02:58.217 --> 00:02:59.612
Independence.

52
00:03:00.617 --> 00:03:03.533
Independence means being able to do things alone.

53
00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.150
Teenagers want more independence.

54
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:09.611
Your turn. Say: Independence.

55
00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:13.630
Independence.

56
00:03:14.383 --> 00:03:15.884
Trust-building.

57
00:03:16.883 --> 00:03:20.230
Trust-building means actions that help people trust each other.

58
00:03:20.817 --> 00:03:22.956
Keeping promises is trust-building.

59
00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.063
Your turn. Say: Trust-building.

60
00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.203
Trust-building.

61
00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.648
Mutual understanding.

62
00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:36.985
Mutual understanding means when both sides understand each other.

63
00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:40.384
Long talks create mutual understanding.

64
00:03:40.983 --> 00:03:43.972
Your turn. Say: Mutual understanding.

65
00:03:46.833 --> 00:03:48.566
Mutual understanding.

66
00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:53.099
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:57.041
Visal, how does your family solve conflicts?

68
00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:01.136
My mother said that we should always talk calmly.

69
00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.377
What did your father say about trust?

70
00:04:05.483 --> 00:04:07.622
He said that trust takes time to build.

71
00:04:08.717 --> 00:04:09.822
Do you agree?

72
00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:15.740
Yes. My grandma told me that empathy creates mutual understanding.

73
00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.505
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:21.640
Grammar focus: Reported speech.

75
00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:23.161
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:26.012
She said that trust takes time to build.

77
00:04:26.917 --> 00:04:28.765
He told me that he was proud of me.

78
00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:31.394
Mum said that we would talk later.

79
00:04:32.333 --> 00:04:38.977
Use 'say' without a person and 'tell' with a person: She said that… / She told me that… Facts that are still true can stay in the present.

80
00:04:39.717 --> 00:04:43.704
Be careful! Don't say: She said me that trust takes time.

81
00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:48.665
Say: She told me that trust takes time.

82
00:04:48.965 --> 00:04:50.662
Say 'told me', not 'said me'.

83
00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:53.956
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:55.919
Talking It Through.

85
00:04:56.219 --> 00:04:59.159
Every family has its own communication style.

86
00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:04.047
My parents said that respect was our most important family value.

87
00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:09.158
Sometimes we have sibling rivalry, but we use conflict resolution.

88
00:05:10.167 --> 00:05:13.211
My father told me that boundaries help everyone feel safe.

89
00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:18.011
Trust-building and empathy bring our family mutual understanding.

90
00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:23.020
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:23.883 --> 00:05:25.651
She blank me that she was tired.

92
00:05:25.951 --> 00:05:29.476
A, told. B, said. C, spoke.

93
00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:34.661
The answer is A: told.

94
00:05:35.817 --> 00:05:39.209
Competition between brothers and sisters is sibling blank.

95
00:05:39.509 --> 00:05:43.128
A, rivalry. B, boundary. C, value.

96
00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:48.887
The answer is A: rivalry.

97
00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:52.386
Understanding how others feel is blank.

98
00:05:52.686 --> 00:05:56.932
A, empathy. B, independence. C, a role model.

99
00:06:00.467 --> 00:06:02.733
The answer is A: empathy.

100
00:06:03.933 --> 00:06:06.911
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:10.713
How do families build trust and resolve conflict?

102
00:06:19.517 --> 00:06:20.947
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:31.887
Families build trust by keeping promises. My father said that we should listen before we speak, so we always talk calmly when there is a conflict.

104
00:06:32.187 --> 00:06:33.978
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:34.883 --> 00:06:38.848
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and reported speech.

106
00:06:39.148 --> 00:06:42.601
Today's value is family. Love and help your family.

107
00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:45.553
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

108
00:06:45.853 --> 00:06:49.376
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

